            <div xml:id="d807">

                <pb facs="0995" n="885" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg885"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/744: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-30T16:00:00+08:00">June 30, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 30—8:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>379. My May 26, noon, from Nanking.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>Lampson informed me today of his Government’s general approval of all he
                        had done in the extraterritoriality negotiations at Nanking except for
                        article 16. He is still awaiting his Government’s reaction on this
                        question.</item>
                    <pb facs="0996" n="886" xml:id="pg886"/>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>He informs me that the British Foreign Secretary will have to make a
                        statement in the House of Commons during the present week regarding the
                        extraterritorial negotiations. The statement is likely to be general in
                        character, with a vague reference to the question of reserved areas. In all
                        probability it will put responsibility for the pause in negotiations upon
                        the Chinese political situation, with specific reference to the Canton
                        crisis.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
